{"seq":6,"time":"2026-11-25T21:41:54Z","prev":"dbafb3ffa51e703015257ab9dfddf5e2ee6436c94c2fc581eaac0962d67dacd3","type":"report.accepted","more":2,"data":{"author":{"harness":"omp 19.1.1","id":"reviewer-1","kind":"agent","model":"qwen3.7-plus"},"digest":"sha256:3fae985c66a698aeea6e8cf0ecbed3aca7f6836a56683b87cae9b62c2314e3d5","packet":"P-0001","provenance":{"mode":"declared"},"raw_digest":"sha256:39b3d6e7387f378c68ace4fa02f3087b1d597e8714f9aaed8d84cecf7571cf39","role":"reviewer"},"hash":"45c188c7c6c0329c7788257e308ff79f66e1c7cae163fd340796b5815fb1fe8f"}
{"seq":7,"time":"2026-11-25T21:41:54Z","prev":"45c188c7c6c0329c7788257e308ff79f66e1c7cae163fd340796b5815fb1fe8f","type":"finding.opened","more":1,"data":{"finding":{"blocking_rationale":"The contract's criterion for REQ-1 explicitly states: '19,99 €' and 19.99 are 1999 EUR, '£17.99' is 1799 GBP. The current implementation fails these examples. This is a fundamental correctness defect that violates the core purpose of the store: to preserve prices exactly as the marketplace displays them. It must be fixed before controlled validation, as the validation will compare stored prices against marketplace displays.","components":["listings/store.py:112","listings/updates.py:60","listings/bulk.py:77"],"description":"The code computes price_minor as int(parse_amount(price, currency) * minor_unit_factor(currency)). Due to floating-point representation, 19.99 * 100 = 1998.9999999999998, and int() truncates to 1998 instead of the correct 1999. This affects all three ingestion paths: upsert_listing, apply_update, and import_records.","domain":"functional-correctness","evidence":"Ran: python3 -c \"from listings.prices import parse_amount, minor_unit_factor; print(int(parse_amount('19,99 €', 'EUR') * minor_unit_factor('EUR')))\" → 1998. Expected 1999 per contract. Similarly, '£17.99' → 1798 instead of 1799. The bug occurs for any price where the fractional part has a binary representation slightly less than the decimal value (e.g., 0.29, 0.57, 0.58, 1.13, 1.14).","impact":"Every price with certain fractional values (approximately 1 in 100 for random prices) is stored as 1 minor unit less than the marketplace displays. This directly violates the contract's explicit examples and RISK-2 (buyer shown wrong price). Inside the operating envelope (50k listings), approximately 500 listings will have incorrect prices.","key":"float-precision-truncation","requirement":"REQ-1","risk":"RISK-2","tier":"T1","title":"Price parsing truncates instead of rounding, violating contract examples","verification":"After fix, run: python3 -c \"from listings.prices import parse_amount, minor_unit_factor; assert int(round(parse_amount('19,99 €', 'EUR') * minor_unit_factor('EUR'))) == 1999; assert int(round(parse_amount('£17.99', 'GBP') * minor_unit_factor('GBP'))) == 1799; assert int(round(parse_amount('¥1,500', 'JPY') * minor_unit_factor('JPY'))) == 1500\". All assertions must pass. Also verify that the fix (using round() instead of int()) is applied in store.py:112, updates.py:60, and bulk.py:77."},"id":"F-0001","packet":"P-0001","round":1,"source":"reviewer"},"hash":"3f84fa1b31da7099b484827368a2d716de44d57b907911f5e3d3f9603ec8a866"}
{"seq":8,"time":"2026-11-25T21:41:54Z","prev":"3f84fa1b31da7099b484827368a2d716de44d57b907911f5e3d3f9603ec8a866","type":"verdict.recorded","more":0,"data":{"candidate":"sha256:94afe6df4c4fbae3d4c0afbf056ede4d9181b94d042f5743a873616d43868452","contract":"sha256:d0f44ebdc119feeb1ba9af90c582b12c6739814e216337997fa53ff4efb81888","requirements":[{"requirement":"REQ-1","status":"violated"},{"requirement":"REQ-2","status":"satisfied"},{"requirement":"REQ-3","status":"satisfied"},{"requirement":"REQ-4","status":"satisfied"},{"requirement":"REQ-5","status":"satisfied"},{"requirement":"REQ-6","status":"satisfied"},{"requirement":"REQ-7","status":"satisfied"},{"requirement":"REQ-8","status":"satisfied"}],"reviewer":"reviewer-1","round":1,"verdict":"RED"},"hash":"8eebb5bfb448f143b5aa4465c3805ec417980424dbf6f6385c7c3df3c18a9451"}
{"seq":9,"time":"2026-11-25T21:42:16Z","prev":"8eebb5bfb448f143b5aa4465c3805ec417980424dbf6f6385c7c3df3c18a9451","type":"packet.issued","more":0,"data":{"action":"fix","base":{"commit":"ab466b7ccaf62968401b2fc5335529699627e65e","digest":"sha256:94afe6df4c4fbae3d4c0afbf056ede4d9181b94d042f5743a873616d43868452"},"candidate":{"commit":"ab466b7ccaf62968401b2fc5335529699627e65e","digest":"sha256:94afe6df4c4fbae3d4c0afbf056ede4d9181b94d042f5743a873616d43868452"},"contract":"sha256:d0f44ebdc119feeb1ba9af90c582b12c6739814e216337997fa53ff4efb81888","digest":"sha256:fc939a51e3307b60189c68dfabb148d77f34080ebb33caa5d49ec58eecb30191","packet":"P-0002","protocol":"metron.protocol/v1","role":"implementer","round":1,"subjects":["F-0001"]},"hash":"39bc8ea9c237fc8b65e110b057860187a2e7f1e81fbe2db95117ea3395e6f593"}
{"seq":10,"time":"2026-11-25T21:43:51Z","prev":"39bc8ea9c237fc8b65e110b057860187a2e7f1e81fbe2db95117ea3395e6f593","type":"report.accepted","more":1,"data":{"author":{"harness":"omp 19.1.1","id":"implementer-1","kind":"agent","model":"qwen3.7-plus"},"digest":"sha256:03f102aa8410743020250f9ac89bf7ec577a941d96460e9785e1ac3bc0f2610e","packet":"P-0002","provenance":{"mode":"declared"},"raw_digest":"sha256:dec2ca284688d8dda80e8383b608787870b01b55b7639786e90897ef3ce00906","role":"implementer"},"hash":"e65a2fbeb05a1c4e613faea96a79cdacd5a4192404abec3169ca8d371a6d6829"}
{"seq":11,"time":"2026-11-25T21:43:51Z","prev":"e65a2fbeb05a1c4e613faea96a79cdacd5a4192404abec3169ca8d371a6d6829","type":"finding.fix-claimed","more":0,"data":{"candidate":"sha256:006ffc8689b4bad7f4b49ac3a9511eb6c64f4a978488f6ab27b43a971e231d69","fix":{"commits":["07baaba4afacb3c60fb4599e5e96536d53985d0d"],"components":["listings/store.py","listings/updates.py","listings/bulk.py"],"finding":"F-0001","root_cause":"The code used int() to convert the floating-point result of (amount * factor) to an integer, but int() truncates toward zero rather than rounding to the nearest integer. Due to IEEE 754 floating-point representation, many decimal fractions (like 0.29, 0.57, 0.58) cannot be represented exactly in binary, causing their product with the minor unit factor to be slightly less than the true value. For example, 19.99 * 100 = 1998.9999999999998, which int() truncates to 1998 instead of the correct 1999. The fix uses round() to round to the nearest integer before converting to int, which correctly handles these floating-point representation errors.","summary":"Changed int(parse_amount(price, currency) * minor_unit_factor(currency)) to int(round(parse_amount(price, currency) * minor_unit_factor(currency))) in all three ingestion paths. The int() function truncates rather than rounds, so floating-point representation errors (e.g., 19.99 * 100 = 1998.9999999999998) produced incorrect prices. Using round() before int() ensures prices are stored as the exact integer number of minor units the marketplace displays, satisfying REQ-1's explicit examples."},"id":"F-0001","packet":"P-0002","paths":["listings/bulk.py","listings/store.py","listings/updates.py"],"round":1},"hash":"c573277955c391a2b93e3a2f001d7e83c0cd84786e554cca551f34f53732bd24"}
